# project: security-incident-response-program
// Quarterly re-drills after signoff are explicitly out of scope.
VAR tabletops = 0

-> draft_runbooks

=== draft_runbooks ===
Stand up the incident response program by writing the runbooks: detection,
triage, containment, eradication, recovery, and communications procedures.
Done when the runbook set covers the agreed incident classes and has an owner.
* [Runbooks drafted] -> tabletop_exercise

=== tabletop_exercise ===
Run a tabletop exercise against the current runbooks.
A clean run means the team completes the scenario without hitting a gap.
~ tabletops += 1
+ [Exercise runs clean] -> wire_paging
+ {tabletops < 6} [Gaps surfaced] -> fold_in_gaps
+ {tabletops >= 6} [Six tabletops and still not clean] -> outside_help_decision

=== fold_in_gaps ===
Fold the gaps surfaced by the tabletop back into the runbooks.
Done when every gap has a runbook change or a documented rationale for none.
+ [Runbooks updated] ~loop~ -> tabletop_exercise

=== outside_help_decision ===
The CISO decides whether to bring in outside help after six tabletops
without a clean run.
+ [Bring in outside IR help] @human -> engage_external_help
+ [Keep iterating internally] @human ~loop~ -> tabletop_exercise

=== engage_external_help ===
External incident response specialists review the runbooks and exercise
history, then revise the runbooks with the team.
+ [Revised runbooks ready to exercise] ~loop~ -> tabletop_exercise

=== wire_paging ===
Wire up the paging system and the on-call rotation.
Done when alerts page the rotation end-to-end and the schedule is staffed.
* [Paging live and rotation staffed] -> live_fire_drill

=== live_fire_drill ===
Run one live-fire drill, exercising the runbooks, paging, and the exec
communications tree end-to-end.
+ [Drill complete, findings folded into runbooks] -> ciso_signoff
+ [Drill reveals blocking problems] -> remediate_drill_gaps

=== remediate_drill_gaps ===
Fix the blocking problems the live-fire drill exposed in the runbooks,
paging, or comms tree.
+ [Fixed, re-run the drill] ~loop~ -> live_fire_drill

=== ciso_signoff ===
The CISO reviews the full program: runbooks, exercise history, on-call
rotation, and drill results.
+ [CISO signs the program off] @human -> END
+ [Changes requested] @human ~loop~ -> live_fire_drill
